## Decisions Made
- Automated reviewer telemetry is collected in a trap-safe best-effort subshell so telemetry failures cannot override settled checks and review threads.
- Failed telemetry is exposed as telemetry_available:false with unavailable provider states instead of being silently discarded.

## Problems Encountered
- Malformed optional CodeRabbit status data caused snapshot to return invalid_github_response: the collector is now isolated from the authoritative snapshot path.
- The first isolation attempt leaked the captured error JSON to successful stderr: stderr suppression was moved onto the isolated collector call and the regression suite was rerun cleanly.

## Constraints Identified
- Selected check and review-thread queries remain hard dependencies because they determine the clean verdict.
- The telemetry subshell must disable inherited cleanup traps so a failed optional query cannot release the parent snapshot lock.

## Open Questions
None

## Context
The shipping-pr runner previously treated automated reviewer telemetry as advisory for verdicts but still failed the entire snapshot when a telemetry API response was malformed. This change isolates telemetry collection, reports its availability explicitly, and preserves checks plus unresolved review threads as the authoritative completion inputs. A deterministic regression now proves malformed optional telemetry still yields clean when checks pass and no actionable thread exists.

